Subject: [202505] Skip unused Buster and Bullseye build environments

The selected docker-sonic-vs.gz, sonic-vs.img.gz and sonic-broadcom.bin
targets do not require Buster or Bullseye runtime layers. The VS PTF images
use Buster; optional SDK and management test images use Bullseye. These are
separate targets, not part of the three selected outputs.
Upstream configure nevertheless initializes every enabled build environment;
its legacy defaults fail on missing security repositories/package archives.

Use upstream NOBUSTER/NOBULLSEYE switches instead of changing mirrors or
removing image dependencies. Keep Bookworm enabled. Explicit NOBUSTER=0
or NOBULLSEYE=0 still permits callers to request a legacy environment.

Failures: https://github.com/ITJamie/sonic-vs-builder/actions/runs/42684597504
          https://github.com/ITJamie/sonic-vs-builder/actions/runs/42688066704
Upstream source: https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-buildimage/blob/ff3c0c9f686a1d0dbddbe813b233b3b7a51bd8e2/Makefile
Verified against ff3c0c9f686a1d0dbddbe813b233b3b7a51bd8e2.
Remove once upstream defaults both switches to 1. Reassess if selected
image dependencies require a legacy environment; this does not port the
optional PTF, SDK or management test images.

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@
 
 NOJESSIE ?= 1
 NOSTRETCH ?= 1
-NOBUSTER ?= 0
-NOBULLSEYE ?= 0
+NOBUSTER ?= 1
+NOBULLSEYE ?= 1
 NOBOOKWORM ?= 0
 
